      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have many many issues with how the current avatar bits work--specifically with OSC. It is extremely difficult to have lots of OSC avatar parameters and to be forced to use the 8 bit SIGNED floats/ints (which usually wastes a bit) when constrained to the 256 avatar parameter limit. Being able to choose the bit precision and to also choose whether or not it's signed would be a genuine godsend. Plus I always want to save up on avatar memory usage, especially for assets I decide to distribute.\n\nBeing able to choose between 1-32 bits of precision would be great, preferably, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 -> 16 -> 24 -> 32\n\nSuper necro bump, sorry.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
